{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Why, etc. — and they kept them alive, etc.</b> One must examine what is the deed they did concerning which he says <b>why have you done</b>; for if they did not kill the children, that would be called negating a deed, and it should have said 'why did you not do.' Further, one must examine his saying <b>and they kept alive</b> — and if he is speaking of providing food for the children, as we explained in connection with his saying 'and the midwives feared, etc. and they kept alive,' etc., if this is what he intended, what answer is there in the midwives' language for this, when they are rebelling against the king?" "Or perhaps it is because Pharaoh did not know explicitly that they were supplying food to the children, for presumably they would not do so openly before the Egyptians, and the children of Israel cannot be suspected of being informers, as they said, may their memory be for blessing (Leviticus Rabbah 32:5), on the verse 'and a woman shall ask, etc.' — for twelve months this matter continued among them and no person ever revealed it. Rather, the Egyptians told him that the midwives were supplying water and food to the houses of the living women, and this matter the neighboring nations are able to recognize, for when the midwife brings in with her items of supply, they know; and they knew also that the living women had borne male children. Therefore Pharaoh said <b>why have you done this thing</b> — meaning, supplying water and food, which is a visible deed. And it is true: if they were not keeping the children alive, I would suppose that you supply them for the daughters; but since the supply goes to the place of the children and the children are alive, this is your sign that it is for them you supply. And this is his saying <b>and you kept the children alive</b> — and this could only be from rational inference as mentioned, for what was clearly known to him was none other than the act of supplying the birthing mothers."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:21.905647069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}